{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Our Sages said: while Noah was in the ark, he set it in his heart and said, 'Who would grant that my sons have slaves, that they sit while slaves minister before them.' And he said, 'When I leave here, whatever I sire I will make slaves.' Canaan went and castrated him. Noah said: You prevented me from siring a fourth son to make him a slave for your brothers — your fourth son shall be a slave to his brothers. And if you ask: why did he curse Canaan more than all the other sons of Ham? According to the one who says 'he castrated him,' it works out, as explained. But according to the one who says 'Ham sodomized him' — what can you say? And the sage Rabbi Aharon found in a midrash that Ham saw and told his brothers mockingly, and did not act in a respectful manner. But it was revealed in the marketplace, and Canaan the despicable heard and sodomized him. Thus it is written: את אשר עשה לו בנו הקטן של חם — 'what his youngest son of Ham did to him' — for the sons of sons are like sons, since Ham himself was not the youngest, for Scripture counts him as the middle one. Rather, it means the youngest of Ham, and that is Canaan. Therefore it is written וירא חם אבי כנען — 'Ham the father of Canaan' — the father of transgression. And according to the one who says 'he castrated him,' he calls Ham 'his youngest son,' that is, the despised one, as in: הנה קטן נתתיך בגוים. And further we say in the chapters of Rabbi Eliezer: what did he see to curse his son with slavery? As it is written: בן יכבד אב ועבד אדניו. This is the meaning: if a son honors his father, well and good; and if not, he shall be a slave to his master. Another interpretation: therefore he cursed him with slavery, because he was the first who saw the matter and the obligation was upon him — that servant-status — and he did not do it, and instead subjugated his brothers to do it. Therefore he was cursed with slavery, measure for measure. And therefore it is also written עבד עבדים — two slaveries: Ham subjugated his brothers, and Canaan subjugated his brothers." "<b>A slave of slaves.</b> Who never goes free to liberty. And what caused him all this curse? That he disgraced his father. And likewise the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to exact punishment from his sons and disgrace them, as it is written: את שבי מצרים ואת גלות כוש נערים וזקנים יחדיו ערום ויחף וחשופי שת ערות מצרים — that He will lead them in disgrace, naked. But Japheth, who honored his father — the El paid him: when Gog and Magog come, the Holy One, blessed be He, will humble them and cover him, as it is said: והיה ביום ההוא אתן לגוג שם מקור קבר. And also He paid the sons of Shem: when the sons of Aaron entered to offer the sacrifice, their souls were burned but not their bodies and not their garments, because they were of the grandsons of Shem. And also when Sennacherib king of Assyria was burned, he was burned without his garments, because he was of his seed."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The text appears slightly disordered: the castration midrash is introduced before 'And if you ask,' and the flow of 'Cananan went and castrated him' may be out of sequence relative to the framing question. Translated as it stands.", 1 "Bracketed variant (וחם)/(וגם) rendered as 'And also,' following the bracketed reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:26.673717773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}